# A name bound to what the language's own code computes of names, with no call, stands for those names (#328), and
# the body's own code reads those names where it reads the name, never where it binds it (#343): `named` binds the gap
# between the level and the module's quiet level (`first.db - QUIET.db`) and the array of both (`const both: Level[] =
# [first, QUIET]`, whose type is written) to names before it hands each to a step, and `written` writes each where its
# step is handed it. An operator is no occurrence and a name adds no arrow, so the two routes are one plan: each step
# takes the level and the quiet level, which alone comes from beyond, and the route's own arrow reads neither where the
# body binds a name to them.

route signal.named
step named/draw
step named/show

line entry > named call
line Level·first > named value
line Level·first > named/draw value                  # `draw(gap)`, `const gap = first.db - QUIET.db`
line Level·QUIET > named/draw value                  # the module's quiet level, from beyond
line Level·first > named/show value                  # `show(both)`, `const both: Level[] = [first, QUIET]`
line Level·QUIET > named/show value
line named/draw > Screen own
line named/show > Screen own

home Level·first named
home Level·QUIET named

side entry left
side Screen right

route signal.written
step written/draw
step written/show

line entry > written call
line Level·first > written value
line Level·first > written/draw value                # `draw(first.db - QUIET.db)`
line Level·QUIET > written/draw value
line Level·first > written/show value                # `show([first, QUIET])`
line Level·QUIET > written/show value
line written/draw > Screen own
line written/show > Screen own

home Level·first written
home Level·QUIET written

side entry left
side Screen right
